Z||000000||fotofrank||06-14-2000||05:32 PM||||Ok friends,how does one installa new muffler on their Fiero? The Dynomax I got on the web will fit but it doesnot have the brackets for the springs that hold the stock muffler. I sure do not want to re-invent the wheel(or in this case muffler hanger) so I'm asking the Forum for advice.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Linx||06-15-2000||10:28 PM||||well- some of the other motor heads are probably gonna freak when i say this but...<P>why bother doing a muffler yourself?  I took mine to midas.  yep- they had fiero mufflers.  New pipe all the way from the cat to the tips. $170.  Lifetime warrenty.  and sounds real good.  I never broke a sweat.  Compare Midas to a new rig from the FieroStore and you'll see it's a great deal.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 06-15-2000).]||||reg||1
